ags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#counting-diff-ediff1d-clip-allclose-isclose-count_nonzero-trace","content":"`cov` and `corrcoef` compute in float64 regardless of the input dtype, so their real\nbill is `2×` the formulas above."},"2407":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1161","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"**Family rule: every write is metered; the access *pattern* sets the weight.**"},"2408":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1162","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"This family used to be uniformly free (pure relocation/selection bought a 0 bill). It\nis not any more: a materializing copy writes real memory and is charged weight 1.0; a\ncomputed-index gather reads via a non-sequential pattern and is charged weight 4.0\n(the access tier); only genuine views stay free. `flop_cost`\nis the count of elements actually **written** — for the triangular/diagonal family\nthat is fewer than the whole array (e.g. `eye`'s off-diagonal zeros are free), not the\nwhole buffer indiscriminately."},"2409":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1163","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"**Materializing copy (weight 1.0, `flop_cost = numel(output)`)** — assembles a new\nbuffer by copying or rearranging existing values sequentially: `concatenate`, `stack`,\n`hstack`, `vstack`, `column_stack`, `dstack`, `block`, `bmat`, `tile`, `repeat`,\n`resize`, `roll`, `insert`, `append`, `delete`, `concat`, `fromiter` (materializes an\niterable into an array, one write per element). `row_stack` bills exactly `vstack`'s\ncost — it is a bare `return vstack(tup)` with no `deduct()` of its own, so its own\nweight entry is inert by construction. `reshape`, `ravel`, `copy`, and `require` are\nbilled `numel(input)` regardless of whether NumPy itself returns a view or a copy for\nthat call — see Views and metadata for why the\ncautious, always-charged price was chosen over trying to detect the view case.\n`flatten` (the ndarray method — there is no free-standing `fnp.flatten` function) is\nalways a genuine copy, never a view, and is billed the same `numel(input)` under the\n`copy` op name. `fft.fftshift`/`fft.ifftshift` are `numpy.roll` under the hood — a\ndata-movement reindex, not part of the FFT priced-in family (see FFT)."},"2410":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1164","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"**Triangular / diagonal writes (weight 1.0)** — bill only the cells that survive, not\nthe whole array:"},"2411":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1165","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"Op"},"2412":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1166","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"flop\\_cost"},"2413":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1167","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"basis"},"2414":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1168","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model#copy-and-gather","content":"`triu`"},"2415":{"id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model-1169","page_id":"/docs/understanding/flop-counting-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/understa