.4):"],[1562,"Billing follows the loop numpy actually runs, in both directions: an explicit narrow\n`dtype=` — pointwise, or a reduction's accumulator — bills narrow because the arithmetic\ngenuinely happens at that width, trading precision for a cheaper bill exactly as\nrequested. `out=` alone never narrows a loop, so it cannot be used to buy a narrow bill\nfor wide compute. The width-rate and complex-factor pricing above is what makes packing\na loss or a break-even; there is no separate dtype-request rule needed to close it."],[1249,"Billing model & design principles"],[2506,"bills like `copy` — no longer a value-test exception, same formula as any other cast"],[2764,"Binary"],[1493,"binary float-only ufuncs except division (`arctan2`, `hypot`, `logaddexp`, …)"],[993,"Binary pointwise ops and broadcasting"],[1110,"Binary pointwise ops keep only the symmetry present in **both** operands. For\ngeneral groups, that means element-set intersection on matching output axes,\nnot just matching tuples of axis numbers."],[1067,"binary pointwise ops keep the intersection of both operands' groups"],[254,"Blacklisted"],[2747,"Blacklisted operations"],[79,"Blocked: `geterr`, `seterr`, `savetxt`, `loadtxt`, and 27 others. These raise\n`AttributeError`. (`save`/`load`/`savez`/`savez_compressed` are supported and\npickle-free — see the Saving & Loading guide.)"],[2834,"Both are LRU-cached; warm-call latency is in microseconds. See `flops.einsum_cache_info()` and `flops.reduction_cache_info()` for cache state."],[384,"Both cross-package pins (`flopscope-server==X.Y.Z` in flopscope's\n`server` extra, and `flopscope==X.Y.Z` in flopscope-server's\n`dependencies`)"],[478,"Both flat and namespaced summaries are constructed in `O(K)` time for the\noperation and optional namespace buckets returned, independent of historical\ncall count. `budget_summary()` and `budget.summary()` format those same mappings.\nOpting into `by_namespace=True` adds the namespace breakdown without changing\nthe